From: Hermes <hermes@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: qcom_scm: add AYN Odin3 to QSEECOM allowlist

QSEECOM is required for ZAP shader loading which brings the GPU's
command processor out of secure mode. Without QSEECOM the Adreno 830
stays locked, Turnip fails with "CP group not found", and all GL
rendering falls back to softpipe.

Add "ayn,odin3" to the machine allowlist so that QSEECOM interfaces
are properly initialized on the Odin3.

Signed-off-by: Hermes <hermes@localhost>
---
diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
index xxxxxxx..yyyyyyy 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2288,6 +2288,7 @@
  */
 static const struct of_device_id qcom_scm_qseecom_allowlist[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "asus,vivobook-s15" },
+	{ .compatible = "ayn,odin3" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,vivobook-s15-x1p4" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,zenbook-a14-ux3407qa" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,zenbook-a14-ux3407ra" },
